        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0658" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg602"/>

                <head>No. 326.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Comanos to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Agency and Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Cairo, Egypt</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1876-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 21, 1876</date>. (Received May 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to announce the unexpected
                    return of H. H. Hassan Pasha, third son of the Khedive, from the Abyssinian
                    expedition on the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>It is rumored that the Egyptian forces have been defeated with great <pb
                        facs="0659" n="603" xml:id="pg603"/> loss. Prince Hassan complains of the
                    cowardice of the Egyptian troops, many of whom threw down their arms and fled
                    when attacked by the Abyssinians.</p>
                <p>His Highness the Khedive has called out the Bashi Bazouks and Bedouin, irregular
                    troops, and dispatched them to the seat of war.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>N. D. COMANOS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul-General, in
                            charge</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
